__pycache__/
*.pyc
dist/
build/
obj_*/
*.zip
*.dll
*.exe
*.obj
*.exp
*.lib

# session backups and build logs
*.pre_*
*.log

# Upstream's header-only dependencies, placed before the first build and
# never ours to commit: plugin_build/build.bat compiles against them via
# /I "include" and builds YYTK_Shared_Types.cpp alongside ModuleMain.cpp, but
# they belong to Aurie Framework and YYToolkit (both AGPL-3.0).
# tools/fetch_toolchain.py places them (README.md's "Building the plugin");
# this stops them showing up as untracked afterwards, which in a full toolkit
# checkout also leaves the super-repo reporting ForgePact as dirty forever.
plugin_build/include/

# Decompiler / disassembler artifacts - never committed, per the hub's
# AGENTS.md "Legal: Decompiled Output Never Reaches Any Origin": reading the
# game in Ghidra/IDA/UndertaleModTool locally is fine, its output stays on the
# researcher's machine. This repository is its own origin and inherits none of
# the hub's .gitignore, so the backstop is repeated here. Our own
# tools/ghidra/ImportSymbols.java stays tracked; a local ghidra_scripts/
# directory (where a decompile helper script lives) does not.
*.i64
*.idb
*.idb0
*.idb1
*.til
*.gpr
*.rep/
**/ghidra_projects/
**/ghidra_scripts/
**/UndertaleModTool_Export/
**/decompiled/
**/disassembly/
*.dis
